          "id": 17592186119771,
          "title": "Describing a Triangular Matrix"
        },
        "markdown": "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
        "mathAcademyId": "e-4394",
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} \\\\ 6 & -1 & {\\color{blue}0} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: $a_{21}=6 \\neq 0.$",
        "status": "completed",
        "stepId": "17592186120619",
        "title": "Describing a Triangular Matrix"
      },
      "total": 4
    },
